# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because a deferred import evaluates the external module `ext-lazy`, and `esm` output imports that module at the start of the chunk. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as d from './d.js';
   │ ─────────────────┬────────────────  
   │                  ╰────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

# Assets

## main.js

```js
import "ext-inner";
import { value } from "ext-lazy";
import { join } from "node:path";
import "ext-eager";
// d.js
const x = [value, join];
// main.js
const read = () => x;
export { read };

```

# Variant: [format: Iife] [name: "lib"]

## warnings

### UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because a deferred import evaluates the external module `ext-lazy`, and `iife` output gets that module as a global or as a wrapper argument. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as d from './d.js';
   │ ─────────────────┬────────────────  
   │                  ╰────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

## Assets

### main.js

```js
var lib = (function(exports, ext_lazy, node_path) {
	Object.defineProperty(exports, Symbol.toStringTag, { value: "Module" });
	// d.js
	const x = [ext_lazy.value, node_path.join];
	// main.js
	const read = () => x;
	exports.read = read;
	return exports;
})({}, ExtLazy, NodePath);

```

# Variant: [format: Umd] [name: "lib"]

## warnings

### UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because a deferred import evaluates the external module `ext-lazy`, and `umd` output gets that module as a global or as a wrapper argument. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as d from './d.js';
   │ ─────────────────┬────────────────  
   │                  ╰────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

